[1m[38;5;231mShould the username be logged?[0m

[38;5;153m❯[39m [38;5;246m1.[39m [38;5;153mYes, log it (Recommended)[39m
     [38;5;246mKeeps the correlation you need to tie a user's bug report to a log line. Matches current behavior, but makes it a [39m
     [38;5;246mdeliberate choice recorded in the spec.[39m
  [38;5;246m2.[39m Redact it too
     [38;5;246mTreat username as PII alongside the password. Safest, but you lose the main handle for tracing a specific user's [39m
     [38;5;246mfailure.[39m
  [38;5;246m3.[39m Log a hash of it
     [38;5;246mCorrelate sessions without storing the identifier in cleartext. You can match log lines to each other, but not back
[39m     [38;5;246mto a user without the original.[39m
